#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:-1
msgid "How to use soft proofing in Krita."
msgstr "Hur bildskärmskorrektur används i Krita."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:0
msgid ".. image:: /images/softproofing/Softproofing_adaptationstate.png"
msgstr ".. image:: /images/softproofing/Softproofing_adaptationstate.png"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:11
msgid "Color"
msgstr "Färg"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:11
msgid "Softproofing"
msgstr "Bildskärmskorrektur"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:16
msgid "Soft Proofing"
msgstr "Bildskärmskorrektur"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:19
msgid ""
"Soft Proofing works only with :ref:`Canvas Graphics Acceleration "
"<display_settings>` enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:21
msgid ""
"When we make an image in Krita, and print that out with a printer, the image "
"tends to look different. The colors are darker, or less dark than expected, "
"maybe the reds are more aggressive, maybe contrast is lost. For simple "
"documents, this isn’t much of a problem, but for professional prints, this "
"can be very sad, as it can change the look and feel of an image drastically."
msgstr ""
"När vi skapar en bild i Krita och skriver ut den på en skrivare, brukar "
"bilden se annorlunda ut. Färgerna är mörkare, eller inte så mörka som "
"förväntat, kanske rött är mer aggressivt, kanske kontrast går förlorad. För "
"enkla dokument är det inte ett så stort problem, med för professionella "
"trycksaker kan det vara mycket ledsamt, eftersom det kan ändra bildens "
"utseende och känsla drastiskt."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:23
msgid ""
"The reason this happens is simply because the printer uses a different color "
"model (CMYK) and it has often access to a lower range of colors (called a "
"gamut)."
msgstr ""
"Orsaken det inträffar är helt enkelt eftersom skrivaren använder en annan "
"färgmodell (CMYK) och ofta har tillgång till ett mindre färgintervall (som "
"kallas färgomfång)."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:25
msgid ""
"A naive person would suggest the following solution: do your work within the "
"CMYK color model! But there are three problems with that:"
msgstr ""
"En naiv person skulle föreslå följande lösning: arbeta inom CMYK "
"färgmodellen! Men det finns tre problem med det:"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:27
msgid ""
"Painting in a CMYK space doesn’t guarantee that the colors will be the same "
"on your printer. For each combination of Ink, Paper and Printing device, the "
"resulting gamut of colors you can use is different, which means that each of "
"these could have a different profile associated with them."
msgstr ""
"Att måla i en CMYK rymd garanterar inte att färgerna blir likadana på "
"skrivaren. För varje kombination av bläck, papper och skrivarenhet, är det "
"resulterande färgomfånget som kan användas annorlunda, vilket betyder att "
"var och en av dem kan ha en annorlunda profil associerad med dem."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:28
msgid ""
"Furthermore, even if you have the profile and are working in the exact color "
"space that your printer can output, the CMYK color space is very irregular, "
"meaning that the color maths isn’t as nice as in other spaces. Blending "
"modes are different in CMYK as well."
msgstr ""
"Dessutom, även om man har profilen och arbetar med exakt den färgrymd som "
"skrivaren kan producera, är CMYK färgrymden mycket oregelbunden, vilket "
"betyder att färgmatematiken inte är så trevlig som i andra färgrymder. "
"Blandningslägen är också annorlunda i CMYK."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:29
msgid ""
"Finally, working in that specific CMYK space means that the image is stuck "
"to that space. If you are preparing your work for different a CMYK profile, "
"due to the paper, printer or ink being different, you might have a bigger "
"gamut with more bright colors that you would like to take advantage of."
msgstr ""
"Slutligen, att arbeta i den specifika CMYK rymden betyder att bilden är fast "
"i den rymden. Om man förbereder sitt arbete för en annan CMYK profil, på "
"grund av att pappret, skrivaren eller bläcket är annorlunda, kan man ha en "
"större färgomfång med starkare färger som man skulle vilja dra fördel av."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:31
msgid ""
"So ideally, you would do the image in RGB, and use all your favorite RGB "
"tools, and let the computer do a conversion to a given CMYK space on the "
"fly, just for preview. This is possible, and is what we call ''Soft "
"Proofing''."
msgstr ""
"Idealiskt bör man skapa bilden i RGB, använda alla sina favoritverktyg i "
"RGB, och låta datorn göra en konvertering till en given CMYK rymd i farten, "
"bara som förhandsgranskning. Det är möjligt, och är vad vi kallar "
"\"Bildskärmskorrektur\"."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:37
msgid ".. image:: /images/softproofing/Softproofing_regularsoftproof.png"
msgstr ".. image:: /images/softproofing/Softproofing_regularsoftproof.png"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:37
msgid ""
"On the left, the original, on the right, a view where soft proofing is "
"turned on. The difference is subtle due to the lack of really bright colors, "
"but the soft proofed version is slightly less blueish in the whites of the "
"flowers and slightly less saturated in the greens of the leaves."
msgstr ""
"Till vänster, originalet, och till höger en vy där bildskärmskorrektur är "
"aktiverad. Differensen är subtil på grund av avsaknaden av riktigt starka "
"färger, men korrekturversionen är något mindre blåaktig i blommornas vita "
"färg och något mindre mättad i lövens gröna färg."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:39
msgid ""
"You can toggle soft proofing on any image using the :kbd:`Ctrl + Y` "
"shortcut. Unlike other programs, this is per-view, so that you can look at "
"your image non-proofed and proofed, side by side. The proofing configuration "
"can also be set per image, and saved into the ``.kra`` file. Just enable :"
"guilabel:`Store Softproofing configuration in the image` in the proofing "
"options in :menuselection:`Image --> Image Properties --> Soft Proofing`. If "
"the checkbox is unchecked, then Krita will use global settings from :"
"menuselection:`Settings --> Configure Krita... --> Color Management --> Soft "
"Proofing` (for more details see :ref:`here "
"<color_management_settings_softproofing>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:42
msgid ""
"When :guilabel:`Store Softproofing configuration in the image` is enabled, "
"Krita embeds the entire proofing ICC profile into ``.kra`` file. This ICC "
"profile can be big for some output devices, especially CMYK ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:44
msgid "There you can set the following options:"
msgstr "Där ser man följande alternativ:"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:47
msgid "Model, Profile"
msgstr "Modell, profil"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:47
msgid ""
"Of these, only the profile is really important. This will serve as the "
"profile you are proofing to. In a professional print workflow, this profile "
"should be determined by the printing house."
msgstr ""
"Av dessa är bara profilen riktigt viktig. Den fungerar som profilen som "
"korrekturen gäller. I ett professionellt arbetsflöde för trycksaker, bör "
"profilen bestämmas av tryckeriet."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:50
msgid ""
"Set the intent used to convert the image to the **proofed output device** "
"profile. It uses the same options as the intents mentioned in the :ref:"
"`color managed workflow <color_managed_workflow>`. This intent should "
"coincide with the conversion intent used by your print house before "
"printing. If your print house does not do any conversion internally, then "
"you should perform the conversion yourself before sending the file to them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:56
msgid "Rendering Intent"
msgstr "Återgivningsalternativ"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:56
msgid ""
"Left: Soft proofed image with Absolute Intent Chromatic Adaptation enabled. "
"Right: Soft proofed image with Absolute Intent Chromatic Adaptation disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:59
msgid "Black Point Compensation"
msgstr "Svartpunktskompensering"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:59
msgid ""
"Enables the black point compensation when converting image to the **proofed "
"output device** profile. Turning this off will clip the shadow values to the "
"minimum that either the screen and the proofing profile can handle, while "
"turning this on will scale the black to the screen-range, showing you the "
"full range of grays in the image. Like :guilabel:`Conversion Rendering "
"Intent`, this value should coincide with the value used by the printing "
"house when performing conversion to the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:62
msgid ""
"Defines the way how the proofed (and possibly clipped) space will be shown "
"on the screen, i.e. what rendering intent and flags will be used to convert "
"colors from the **proofed output device** profile into the **screen** "
"profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:64
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Use global display settings` instructs Krita to render the "
"proofed space using the global settings, set in :menuselection:`Settings --> "
"Configure Krita... --> Color Management --> Display`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:66
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Simulate paper white and black` is used to preview the white "
"point (or \"color tint\") of the paper on the current display. In other "
"words, if the paper is matte, or metallic, or has some sort of sepia effect, "
"this will be visible on your screen. Please take it into account that the "
"viewing conditions' white point will still be adjusted to the one of the "
"screen. It means that you cannot visually compare the physical print and the "
"image on the screen, unless all three white points coincide: the one in the "
"paper profile, the one the display is configured to and the white point of "
"the light bulb that illuminates your physical print."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:68
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Custom` allows you to configure the final conversion step "
"manually. You may want to configure the pipeline depending on your goal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:71
msgid ":guilabel:`Rendering Intent` --> :guilabel:`Relative Colorimetric`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:72
msgid ":guilabel:`Black Point Compensation` --> `Enabled`"
msgstr ":guilabel:`Svartpunktskompensering` --> `Aktiverad`"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:74
msgid "Preview color gamut (or \"color variety\") of the image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:74
msgid ""
"If you want to use :guilabel:`Out of Gamut Warnings`, it is best to use them "
"in this mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:77
msgid ":guilabel:`Rendering Intent` --> :guilabel:`Absolute Colorimetric`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:78
msgid ":guilabel:`Absolute Intent Chromatic Adaptation` --> `Enabled`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:81
msgid ""
"If you are using Wayland compositor, Absolute Colorimetric intent may be "
"**broken** (even in XWayland mode). More than that, it may be broken "
"differently in different versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:83
msgid ""
"In KWin 6.4.x and earlier, :guilabel:`Absolute Colorimetric` will behave as "
"if :guilabel:`Absolute Intent Chromatic Adaptation` is **always disabled**. "
"It will cause severe color tint if white points "
"(`sigChromaticAdaptationTag`) of the printer and display profiles do not "
"coincide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:85
msgid ""
"In KWin 6.5.x and later, :guilabel:`Absolute Colorimetric` will behave as "
"if :guilabel:`Absolute Intent Chromatic Adaptation` is **always enabled**. "
"Given that you **keep the checkbox set**, the feature will work correctly "
"and will let you preview contrast degradations, but you will not be able to "
"get advanced effects of disabling color adaptation to the display space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:87
msgid "Display Mode"
msgstr "Visningsläge"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:87
msgid "Preview contrast degradations caused by the color of the paper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:87
msgid ""
"This is a problem of the Wayland protocol specification, the fix is "
"`discussed here <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/wayland/wayland-protocols/-/"
"merge_requests/439>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:90
msgid "Gamut Warning"
msgstr "Färgomfångsvarning"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:90
msgid "Set the color of :guilabel:`Out of Gamut Warnings`."
msgstr "Ställ in färgen på :guilabel:`färgomfångsvarningar`."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:92
msgid ""
"You can set the defaults that Krita uses in :menuselection:`Settings --> "
"Configure Krita... --> Color Management --> Soft Proofing`."
msgstr ""
"Standardvärden som används av Krita kan ställas in med :menuselection:"
"`Inställningar --> Anpassa Krita... --> Färghantering --> "
"Bildskärmskorrektur`."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:94
msgid ""
"To configure this properly, it's recommended to make a test image to print "
"(and that is printed by a properly set-up printer) and compare against, and "
"then approximate in the proofing options how the image looks compared to the "
"real-life copy you have made."
msgstr ""
"För att ställa in det på ett riktigt sätt, rekommenderas att skapa en "
"testbild att skriva ut (och som skrivs ut av en riktigt inställd skrivare) "
"och jämföra med, och sedan uppskatta i korrekturalternativen hur bilden ser "
"ut jämfört med kopian från verkliga livet."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:97
msgid "Out of Gamut Warning"
msgstr "Varna för utanför färgomfång"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:99
msgid ""
"The out of gamut warning, or gamut alarm, is an extra option on top of Soft-"
"Proofing: It allows you to see which colors are being clipped, by replacing "
"the resulting color with the set alarm color."
msgstr ""
"Varningen för utanför färgomfång, eller färgomfångsalarmet, är ett extra "
"alternativ för bildskärmskorrektur. Det låter dig se vilka färger som "
"beskärs genom att ersätta resultatfärgen med angiven alarmfärg."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:101
msgid ""
"This can be useful to determine where certain contrasts are being lost, and "
"to allow you to change it slowly to a less contrasted image."
msgstr ""
"Det kan vara användbart för att bestämma var vissa kontraster går förlorade, "
"och för att göra det möjligt att långsamt ändra det till en bild med mindre "
"kontrast."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:107
msgid ".. image:: /images/softproofing/Softproofing_gamutwarnings.png"
msgstr ".. image:: /images/softproofing/Softproofing_gamutwarnings.png"

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:107
msgid ""
"Left: View with original image, Right: View with soft proofing and gamut "
"warnings turned on. Krita will save the gamut warning color alongside the "
"proofing options into the KRA file, so pick a color that you think will "
"stand out for your current image."
msgstr ""
"Vänster: Vy med originalbilden. Höger: Vy med bildskärmskorrektur och "
"färgomfångsvarningar aktiverade. Krita sparar färgen för "
"färgomfångsvarningar tillsammans med korrekturalternativen i KRA-filen, så "
"välj en färg som tydligt framträder med den aktuella bilden."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:109
msgid ""
"You can activate Gamut Warnings with the :kbd:`Ctrl + Shift + Y` shortcut, "
"but it needs soft proofing activated to work fully."
msgstr ""
"Man kan aktivera färgomfångsvarningar med genvägen :kbd:`Ctrl + Shift + Y`, "
"men det kräver att bildskärmskorrektur är aktiverad för att fungera "
"fullständigt."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:112
msgid ""
"Soft Proofing doesn’t work properly in floating-point spaces, and attempting "
"to force it will cause incorrect gamut alarms. It is therefore disabled."
msgstr ""
"Bildskärmskorrektur fungerar inte riktigt i flyttalsrymder, och att försöka "
"tvinga fram den skulle orsaka felaktiga färgomfångsalarm. Därför är den "
"inaktiverad."

#: ../../user_manual/soft_proofing.rst:115
msgid ""
"Gamut Warnings sometimes give odd warnings for linear profiles in the "
"shadows. This is a bug in LittleCMS, see `here <https://ninedegreesbelow.com/"
"bug-reports/soft-proofing-problems.html>`_ for more info."
msgstr ""
"Färgomfångsvarningar ger ibland konstiga resultat i skuggorna av linjära "
"profiler. Det är ett fel i LittleCMS, titta `här <https://ninedegreesbelow."
"com/bug-reports/soft-proofing-problems.html>`_ för mer information."

